init (3) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * Before a reboot or halt, init runs /etc/rc.shutdown, for 30 seconds at
    most, while it still serves the bootstrap port.
  * The first reboot or halt request decides which one happens.

 -- Maxwell <maxwell@blueberrypieos.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:16:19 +0000

init (2) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * Start getty on the console in place of a root shell.
  * Only root may check in or register a system service name.
  * Bootstrap requests need a send-once reply port and a send right.
  * A console that fails to start is tried again a second later.
  * init makes the port of com.apple.auditd at boot and sets it as the
    host's audit control port. auditd checks it in. Only root may check it in,
    and no one may look it up.

 -- Maxwell <maxwell@blueberrypieos.com>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:28:13 +0000

